#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This lesson provides an introduction to this course including an overview of"
" the course contents, and approach to learning."
msgstr ""
"Pelajaran ini memberikan pengantar kursus ini termasuk gambaran umum isi "
"kursus, dan pendekatan pembelajaran."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Course introduction"
msgstr "Pengantar kursus"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Course introduction {#course-introduction}"
msgstr "Pengantar kursus {#course-introduction}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This training is designed for both expert and non-expert developers who want"
" to learn about how quantum computing poses a risk to existing cryptography "
"as new quantum algorithms are able to break existing encryption schemes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pelatihan ini dirancang untuk pengembang ahli maupun non-ahli yang ingin "
"belajar tentang bagaimana komputasi kuantum menimbulkan risiko terhadap "
"kriptografi yang ada karena algoritma kuantum baru mampu memecahkan skema "
"enkripsi yang ada.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Specifically, the default information is geared towards individuals with "
"programming knowledge but limited or no experience in cryptography or "
"quantum concepts. Practical Python examples are given which demonstrate the "
"mathematical principles of cryptography, and can be used for some "
"experimentation to improve understanding. This also caters to those seeking "
"a high-level overview of quantum cryptography's workings and its "
"significance in the modern world.\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara khusus, informasi default ditujukan untuk individu dengan pengetahuan"
" pemrograman tetapi pengalaman terbatas atau tidak ada dalam konsep "
"kriptografi atau kuantum. Contoh Python praktis diberikan yang "
"mendemonstrasikan prinsip-prinsip matematis kriptografi, dan dapat digunakan"
" untuk beberapa eksperimen guna meningkatkan pemahaman. Ini juga melayani "
"mereka yang mencari gambaran umum tingkat tinggi tentang cara kerja "
"kriptografi kuantum dan signifikansinya di dunia modern.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Readers desiring a deeper understanding of both quantum physics concepts and"
" cryptography should explore our expandable sections and presentations, "
"which delve into the foundational mathematical concepts of this topic.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pembaca yang menginginkan pemahaman lebih mendalam tentang konsep fisika "
"kuantum dan kriptografi harus mengeksplorasi bagian yang dapat diperluas dan"
" presentasi kami, yang menggali konsep-konsep matematika dasar dari topik "
"ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Through this course, readers will learn how even today's data is at risk as "
"it can be collected now, and decrypted later. It will demonstrate how our "
"existing algorithms are compromised and introduce the innovative techniques "
"which protect against such threats through an <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Set of principles and practices used in software development "
"and project management. It emphasizes flexibility, collaboration, iterative "
"development, and customer involvement throughout the project lifecycle. The "
"goal of the agile approach is to respond quickly to changing requirements, "
"deliver incremental improvements, and achieve better alignment with customer"
" needs.\">agile</DefinitionTooltip> approach.\n"
msgstr ""
"Melalui kursus ini, pembaca akan belajar bagaimana bahkan data hari ini "
"berisiko karena bisa dikumpulkan sekarang, dan didekripsi nanti. Ini akan "
"mendemonstrasikan bagaimana algoritma yang ada menjadi rentan dan "
"memperkenalkan teknik inovatif yang melindungi dari ancaman tersebut melalui"
" pendekatan <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Set of principles and practices "
"used in software development and project management. It emphasizes "
"flexibility, collaboration, iterative development, and customer involvement "
"throughout the project lifecycle. The goal of the agile approach is to "
"respond quickly to changing requirements, deliver incremental improvements, "
"and achieve better alignment with customer "
"needs.\">agile</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Key takeaways for this course {#key-takeaways-for-this-course}"
msgstr "Poin-poin penting kursus ini {#key-takeaways-for-this-course}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "By the end of this course, you will have a better understanding of:\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada akhir kursus ini, Anda akan memiliki pemahaman yang lebih baik "
"tentang:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Cryptographic primitives that underpin current cryptographic systems:\n"
msgstr "Primitif kriptografi yang mendasari sistem kriptografi saat ini:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Cryptographic Hashing\n"
msgstr "Hashing Kriptografis\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Asymmetric Cryptography\n"
msgstr "Kriptografi Asimetris\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Symmetric Cryptography\n"
msgstr "Kriptografi Simetris\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The quantum threat to classical encryption schemes\n"
msgstr "Ancaman kuantum terhadap skema enkripsi klasik\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum-safe encryption schemes\n"
msgstr "Skema enkripsi aman-kuantum\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You will also have had the opportunity, if you wish, to run some example "
"Python code demonstrating some of the approaches.\n"
msgstr ""
"Anda juga akan memiliki kesempatan, jika mau, untuk menjalankan beberapa "
"contoh kode Python yang mendemonstrasikan beberapa pendekatan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Finally you can apply for a badge by passing an exam.\n"
msgstr "Akhirnya Anda bisa mendaftar untuk lencana dengan lulus ujian.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Tips for navigating this course {#tips-for-navigating-this-course}"
msgstr "Tips navigasi kursus ini {#tips-for-navigating-this-course}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this course, you can pace your learning however you prefer. The total "
"duration is approximately 6–7 hours including the additional presentations, "
"and running the sample code, though this time will vary depending on your "
"existing knowledge and any links you follow. If you need to leave the "
"course, you can easily return later.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam kursus ini, Anda bisa mengatur kecepatan belajar sesuai keinginan "
"Anda. Total durasi adalah sekitar 6–7 jam termasuk presentasi tambahan, dan "
"menjalankan kode contoh, meskipun waktu ini akan bervariasi tergantung pada "
"pengetahuan yang sudah Anda miliki dan tautan yang Anda ikuti. Jika Anda "
"perlu meninggalkan kursus, Anda bisa dengan mudah kembali nanti.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can see where you are in the course material using the navigation on the"
" left hand side of the main content. Individual lessons can be expanded to "
"see a set of topics, and you can click to go back to previous topics.\n"
msgstr ""
"Anda bisa melihat di mana Anda berada dalam materi kursus menggunakan "
"navigasi di sisi kiri konten utama. Pelajaran individual dapat diperluas "
"untuk melihat sekumpulan topik, dan Anda bisa klik untuk kembali ke topik "
"sebelumnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Additional References and hover-help can be found highlighted as you go "
"through the material.\n"
msgstr ""
"Referensi tambahan dan hover-help dapat ditemukan yang disorot saat Anda "
"mengerjakan materi.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Before you begin {#before-you-begin}"
msgstr "Sebelum Anda mulai {#before-you-begin}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An introductory presentation is linked from the **Helpful Materials** "
"section on the course overview page.\n"
msgstr ""
"Presentasi pengantar ditautkan dari bagian **Materi yang Berguna** di "
"halaman gambaran umum kursus.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This provides:\n"
" - An introduction to cryptography\n"
" - A maths primer\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini menyediakan:\n"
" - Pengantar kriptografi\n"
" - Primer matematika\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you are unfamiliar with these topics, you may wish to review this "
"presentation before starting the lessons, or return to it if you feel the "
"need later.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika Anda tidak familiar dengan topik-topik ini, Anda mungkin ingin meninjau"
" presentasi ini sebelum memulai pelajaran, atau kembali ke sana jika Anda "
"merasa perlu nanti.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Lesson structure {#lesson-structure}"
msgstr "Struktur pelajaran {#lesson-structure}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each lesson will include:\n"
"- An introduction including the learning objective for this lesson\n"
"- Detail on the cryptography topic being presented including:\n"
"  - An explanation of the the topic and current algorithms\n"
"  - Math explanations and examples. Some of these are in collapsible sections so you can skip if you do not wish to understand the math detail.\n"
"  - Optional Python code examples that can be run (you will need to be logged in)\n"
"  - Risks from classical computing algorithms\n"
"  - Risks from quantum computing algorithms\n"
"  - Approaches to mitigate this risk\n"
"- A list of key takeaways from the lesson\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap pelajaran akan mencakup:\n"
"- Pengantar termasuk tujuan pembelajaran untuk pelajaran ini\n"
"- Detail tentang topik kriptografi yang dipresentasikan termasuk:\n"
"  - Penjelasan tentang topik dan algoritma saat ini\n"
"  - Penjelasan dan contoh matematika. Beberapa di antaranya ada di bagian yang dapat diciutkan sehingga Anda bisa melewatinya jika tidak ingin memahami detail matematis.\n"
"  - Contoh kode Python opsional yang bisa dijalankan (Anda perlu login)\n"
"  - Risiko dari algoritma komputasi klasik\n"
"  - Risiko dari algoritma komputasi kuantum\n"
"  - Pendekatan untuk memitigasi risiko ini\n"
"- Daftar poin-poin penting dari pelajaran\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Running the Python examples {#running-the-python-examples}"
msgstr "Menjalankan contoh Python {#running-the-python-examples}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Python code has been run already so that readers browsing the text can "
"see the results without additional steps. However, and in particular for "
"those with an interest in software development, you are encouraged to run "
"these examples yourself. You can also experiment with input parameters and "
"explore the principles in an experimental way.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kode Python telah dijalankan sebelumnya sehingga pembaca yang menelusuri "
"teks bisa melihat hasilnya tanpa langkah tambahan. Namun, dan terutama bagi "
"mereka yang tertarik dalam pengembangan perangkat lunak, Anda dianjurkan "
"untuk menjalankan contoh-contoh ini sendiri. Kamu juga bisa bereksperimen "
"dengan parameter input dan menjelajahi prinsip-prinsip dengan cara "
"eksperimental.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When you run a Python cell for the first time, you will be prompted to log "
"in to IBM Quantum&reg;.\n"
msgstr ""
"Saat Anda menjalankan sel Python untuk pertama kali, Anda akan diminta untuk"
" login ke IBM Quantum&reg;.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You should run each Python cell in order, from the beginning of the "
"notebook. Later cells are typically dependent on earlier ones to set up "
"libraries, variables, and so on. Each cell has been written to produce some "
"output after execution.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kamu harus menjalankan setiap sel Python secara berurutan, dari awal "
"notebook. Sel-sel selanjutnya biasanya bergantung pada sel-sel sebelumnya "
"untuk menyiapkan pustaka, variabel, dan sebagainya. Setiap sel telah ditulis"
" untuk menghasilkan beberapa output setelah dieksekusi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Important\">\n"
"The Python code examples are provided to demonstrate the mathematical principles of the algorithms being discussed. They are not intended to be used as actual implementations. It is essential to use well-supported and reviewed security libraries in any real-world usage.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Penting\">\n"
"Contoh kode Python diberikan untuk mendemonstrasikan prinsip-prinsip matematis dari algoritma yang sedang dibahas. Mereka tidak dimaksudkan untuk digunakan sebagai implementasi aktual. Sangat penting untuk menggunakan pustaka keamanan yang didukung dan ditinjau dengan baik dalam penggunaan dunia nyata apapun.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Digital Certification {#digital-certification}"
msgstr "Sertifikasi Digital {#digital-certification}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
